I see the issue with `setTheme`:

```ts
setTheme(theme: string): void {
    if (!theme) {
      theme = "tutors";
    }
    if (themeService.themes.find((theme) => theme.name === this.currentTheme.value)) {
      this.currentTheme.value = theme;
    } else {
      this.currentTheme.value = "tutors";
    }
```

The condition `themeService.themes.find((theme) => theme.name === this.currentTheme.value)` is checking if the CURRENT theme (not the new theme) exists in the list. 

So when you call `setTheme("nonexistent-theme")`, it validates whether the current theme exists in the themes list, and if it does, it just sets the new theme without checking if that new theme is actually valid. The logic is backwards — it should be validating the incoming theme, not the current one.

Now I'm looking at the festive test to see how `eventTrigger()` connects to the snow effects.

